    {
      "id": "p0181-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In 1995, Square released Chrono Trigger for the Japanese Super Famicom and the North American Super NES. This classic, influential Japanese RPG introduced new gameplay concepts not found in its contemporaries, including time-travel mechanics, branching storylines, and multi character battle techniques. As the product of a dream team of game developers, Chrono Trigger enjoyed commercial and critical success upon release, and remains well regarded to this day.",
        "raw": "In 1995, Square released Chrono Trigger for the Japanese Super Famicom\nand the North American Super NES. This classic, influential Japanese\nRPG introduced new gameplay concepts not found in its contemporaries,\nincluding time-travel mechanics, branching storylines, and multi\ncharacter battle techniques. As the product of a dream team of game\ndevelopers, Chrono Trigger enjoyed commercial and critical success upon\nrelease, and remains well regarded to this day.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
